# Encrypted signing material is ciphertext, not text. Git can guess "text" for
# a small blob that happens to contain no NUL byte -- signing.env.enc is 144
# bytes and does -- and a checkout under core.autocrlf=true would then rewrite
# its line endings and corrupt it. The damage surfaces in CI at
# `security import` as a complaint about the password, which reads like a
# broken certificate and is nothing of the kind.
*.enc binary
